<!-- Codec2 IComponentStore declarations for this device.
     BOTH stores are declared here, in ONE <hal>, at ONE version, on purpose.
     Read the comment in Android.bp before changing anything below.

     default  is served by vendor.qti.media.c2@1.0-service      (every HW video
              codec on this SoC: avc/hevc/vp9/av1 decode, avc/hevc/heic encode)
     default2 is served by vendor.qti.media.c2audio@1.0-service (QTI audio)

     WHY ONE <hal> AT ONE VERSION: libvintf rejects a second manifest entry for
     the same HIDL HAL name with the same MAJOR version, whatever the minor --
     HalManifest::addingConflictingMajorVersion() keys its map on majorVer alone
     ("Conflicting major version: 1.0 ... vs. 1.2"). So @1.2::.../default and the
     stock fragment's @1.0::.../default2 cannot coexist. Worse, the loser is
     decided by readdir() order: VintfObject::addDirectoryManifests() lists
     /vendor/etc/vintf/manifest/ with FileSystemImpl::listFiles(), which is a
     bare readdir with NO sort, and a fragment that fails to merge aborts the
     WHOLE device manifest fetch. So the stock c2_manifest_vendor_audio.xml is
     not shipped (see proprietary-files.txt) and its instance is declared here.

     WHY @1.2 FOR BOTH: vendor.qti.media.c2@1.0-service registers `default` at
     @1.2 -- observed, not assumed:
       E HidlServiceManagement: Service android.hardware.media.c2@1.2::
         IComponentStore/default must be in VINTF manifest in order to register.
     Declaring @1.0 does NOT satisfy it: HalManifest::forEachInstanceOfVersion()
     matches with Version::minorAtLeast(), so a manifest minor must be >= the
     requested minor. The reverse is fine, which is why @1.2 also serves the
     audio store's @1.0 registration of default2 -- verified live, default2
     registers and contributes 4 codecs.

     WHY override="true": it is the only way past shouldAdd()'s conflict check
     (HalManifest::add() short-circuits on isOverride()), and it clears any
     same-major entry a re-extracted stock fragment would reintroduce, making
     this robust against readdir order rather than dependent on it.

     `software` is deliberately NOT declared: AOSP's own
     system/etc/vintf/manifest/manifest_media_c2_software.xml declares
     @1.2::IComponentStore/software with max-level="8" from the FRAMEWORK
     manifest, which is a separate manifest and cannot conflict with this one. -->
<manifest version="1.0" type="device">
    <hal format="hidl" override="true">
        <name>android.hardware.media.c2</name>
        <transport>hwbinder</transport>
        <fqname>@1.2::IComponentStore/default</fqname>
        <fqname>@1.2::IComponentStore/default2</fqname>
    </hal>
</manifest>
